  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"grant_options\" AND override_eligibility == True AND escalated == False THEN the policy must return (False, \"override_eligibility=True without prior escalation.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"grant_options\" AND override_eligibility == True AND escalated == True AND eligibility_result.eligible == True AND eligibility_result.in_roster == True AND eligibility_result.has_contract == True THEN the policy must return (True, \"grant_options approved.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"grant_options\" AND override_eligibility == False AND eligibility_result.eligible == True AND eligibility_result.in_roster == True AND eligibility_result.has_contract == True THEN the policy must return (True, \"grant_options approved.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND (blackout_result is missing OR blackout_result is not a dict) THEN the policy must return (False, \"Missing or malformed blackout_result for approve_exercise.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND blackout_result.in_blackout == False AND bypass_window_check == False THEN the policy must return (True, …) – exercise is allowed outside a blackout period."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND blackout_result.in_blackout == False AND bypass_window_check == True AND escalated == False THEN the policy must return (False, \"bypass_window_check=True without prior escalation.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND blackout_result.in_blackout == False AND bypass_window_check == True AND escalated == True THEN the policy must return (True, …) – bypass is permitted after escalation."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND blackout_result.in_blackout == True AND bypass_window_check == False THEN the policy must return (False, \"Exercise date falls in blackout period and bypass_window_check is False.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND blackout_result.in_blackout == True AND bypass_window_check == True AND escalated == False THEN the policy must return (False, \"bypass_window_check=True in blackout without prior escalation.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND blackout_result.in_blackout == True AND bypass_window_check == True AND escalated == True THEN the policy must return (True, …) – exercise is allowed with explicit bypass after escalation."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS ∪ HIGH_RISK_TOOLS (i.e., any other tool) THEN the policy defaults to (True, …) – the call is permitted."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF (eligibility_result.eligible == False OR eligibility_result.in_roster == False OR eligibility_result.has_contract == False) AND the next high‑risk call is \"grant_options\" THEN the policy must reject that call (return False) unless the agent first calls reject_request or escalate_to_compliance."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF blackout_result.in_blackout == True AND bypass_window_check == False AND the next high‑risk call is \"approve_exercise\" THEN the policy must reject that call (return False) unless the agent first calls reject_request or escalate_to_compliance."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a user statement (e.g., claim of urgency, hardship, authority, or pasted document) is present but the required tool check (check_employee_eligibility or check_insider_trading_window) has not been performed, the policy does not consider the user statement sufficient and will still enforce the above pre‑conditions for any high‑risk tool."
  }
]

The list enumerates every required pre‑condition (eligibility flags, escalation status, blackout status, and bypass flags) and the corresponding allowed or denied outcomes, mirroring the logic implemented in the `policy` function and the security requirements. Each IF‑THEN clause is directly checkable against the arguments supplied to the policy, ensuring that only properly vetted calls to high‑risk tools are permitted.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"grant_options\" AND eligibility_result.eligible == true AND eligibility_result.in_roster == true AND eligibility_result.has_contract == true AND (override_eligibility == false OR (override_eligibility == true AND escalated == true AND override_approval_granted == true)) THEN the policy returns (True, …) – i.e., the call is allowed."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"grant_options\" AND (eligibility_result is missing OR eligibility_result.eligible != true OR eligibility_result.in_roster != true OR eligibility_result.has_contract != true) THEN the policy returns (False, \"Eligibility check failed …\") – the call is denied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"grant_options\" AND override_eligibility == true AND (escalated != true OR override_approval_granted != true) THEN the policy returns (False, \"override_eligibility=True without prior escalation or explicit approval\") – the call is denied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND blackout_result is missing THEN the policy returns (False, \"Blackout result missing …\") – the call is denied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND bypass_window_check == false AND blackout_result.in_blackout == true THEN the policy returns (False, \"Exercise date falls in blackout period …\") – the call is denied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND bypass_window_check == true AND (escalated != true OR bypass_approval_granted != true) THEN the policy returns (False, \"bypass_window_check=True without prior escalation or explicit bypass approval\") – the call is denied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND bypass_window_check == true AND escalated == true AND bypass_approval_granted == true THEN the policy returns (True, …) – the call is allowed regardless of blackout_result.in_blackout."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name in ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN the policy returns (True, …) – the call is always allowed."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name in HIGH_RISK_TOOLS AND (eligibility_result.eligible == false OR blackout_result.in_blackout == true) AND NOT (tool_name == \"grant_options\" AND override_eligibility == true) AND NOT (tool_name == \"approve_exercise\" AND bypass_window_check == true) THEN the policy returns (False, …) – high‑risk calls are prohibited after a negative check unless a reject_request or escalate_to_compliance is performed first."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF eligibility_result.eligible == false THEN the agent must call either reject_request or escalate_to_compliance before any subsequent call to a tool in HIGH_RISK_TOOLS; otherwise any such high‑risk call will be denied by the policy."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF blackout_result.in_blackout == true THEN the agent must call either reject_request or escalate_to_compliance before any subsequent call to a tool in HIGH_RISK_TOOLS (including approve_exercise without bypass); otherwise the high‑risk call will be denied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a user statement (e.g., urgency claim, hardship claim, authority claim, pasted document) is present in the conversation THEN it does NOT set any of the flags eligibility_checked, blackout_checked, escalated, override_approval_granted, or bypass_approval_granted; the policy still requires the corresponding tool calls and flags to be present."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name is not in ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS AND not in HIGH_RISK_TOOLS THEN the policy returns (False, \"Tool '{tool_name}' is not recognized or is denied by default\") – deny‑by‑default for unknown tools."
  }
]

These IF‑THEN clauses capture every pre‑condition (required flags, eligibility/blackout results, escalation and explicit approvals) and post‑condition (allow or deny) for both permitted and prohibited scenarios, directly reflecting the security request and the consolidated policy requirements.

